`TrainerConfig` regularises fine-tuning. `backbone_dropout` sets every dropout outside the head, attention dropouts included, and REVE, which has no dropout, refuses it. `head_weight_decay` gives the head its own AdamW weight decay, as a skorch parameter group. Both default to `None`, which changes nothing, and can be tuned with a grid such as `trainer__backbone_dropout`. `ExperimentConfig(keep_test_embeddings=True)` keeps, with each outer fold's predictions, the embeddings of its test rows (the fitted estimator's `transform`), so each sample's comes from the one fold that held it out; `ExperimentResult.get_embeddings(model)` returns them with their fold, sample id and group. `FoundationClassifier.transform` returns the fine-tuned embeddings, which for CTNet, Deep4Net, EEGNet and ShallowFBCSPNet are the flattened input of their final layer.
